refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.returnvalues;

 An array containing the current keys of each attached
 iterator. With MultipleIterator::MIT_NEED_ANY, &null;
 is used for the iterators that are not valid.

&reftitle.errors;
Throws a RuntimeException if no iterator is attached, or if MultipleIterator::MIT_NEED_ALL is set and at least one attached iterator is not valid.
Throws an InvalidArgumentException if MultipleIterator::MIT_KEYS_ASSOC is set and an iterator was attached without associated information.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.1.0

     A RuntimeException is now thrown if
     MultipleIterator::key is called when no
     iterator is attached. Previously, &false; was returned.

  &reftitle.examples;

   MultipleIterator::key example


<?php
$iterator = new MultipleIterator(MultipleIterator::MIT_NEED_ANY | MultipleIterator::MIT_KEYS_ASSOC);
$iterator->attachIterator(new ArrayIterator(['a' => 'apple', 'b' => 'banana']), 'fruit');
$iterator->attachIterator(new ArrayIterator(['x' => 'red']), 'color');

$iterator->rewind();
while ($iterator->valid()) {
    var_dump($iterator->key());
    $iterator->next();
}
?>


   &example.outputs;


array(2) {
  ["fruit"]=>
  string(1) "a"
  ["color"]=>
  string(1) "x"
}
array(2) {
  ["fruit"]=>
  string(1) "b"
  ["color"]=>
  NULL
}
